From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 23 Aug 2026 12:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: adreno: drop the GPU DDR vote across system suspend

With per-OPP bandwidth votes wired, the GPU sleeps with its last OPP's
interconnect vote standing. On msm8998 the RPM never applies its sleep
set (no APSS power-collapse handshake), so that active-set vote holds
DDR at the voted rate through every system suspend. Drop the OPP after
pm_runtime_force_suspend(), when the GPU is fully quiescent - zeroing
the bandwidth, level and required-opps votes for the sleep. The OPP is
re-established lazily by the first devfreq target() after resume
(opp_table->enabled is false, so the same-OPP early return does not
trigger). Deliberately not hooked into runtime PM: a first cut in
msm_devfreq_suspend() ran on every screen-off idle and was implicated
in a lock/unlock crash.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
index 28f744f..67dff89 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2014,2017 The Linux Foundation. All rights reserved.
  */
 
+#include <linux/pm_opp.h>
+
 #include "adreno_gpu.h"
 
 bool hang_debug = false;
@@ -379,6 +381,17 @@ out:
 	if (ret)
 		resume_scheduler(gpu);
 
+	/*
+	 * Drop the OPP entirely so the DDR bandwidth vote goes to zero for
+	 * the sleep.  On msm8998 the RPM never applies its sleep set (no
+	 * APSS power-collapse handshake), so a standing active-set vote
+	 * holds DDR at the voted rate through the whole system suspend.
+	 * The OPP is re-established lazily by the first devfreq target()
+	 * after resume; the GPU is fully quiescent here, so nothing races.
+	 */
+	if (!ret)
+		dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, NULL);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
